$0(){return A.hG(this.a,"# Meeseeks Box \u2014 one templated word, summoned into a chord. Proof of meta: params.\nname Meeseeks Box\n#\n# `meta: meeseeks n \u2026` defines a voice with one param `n`. Each `meeseeks <num>`\n# call replays the body with n -> <num>, so the number is the oscillator's id AND\n# its frequency \u2014 one definition, four distinct voices. Meeseeks exist to serve.\n\nmeta: meeseeks n filter ClassicOscillator n \\\n  knob n freq n \\\n  knob n waveform 2\n\n# Summon the box: same word, four params -> four distinct oscillators (C3 G3 C4 G4).\nmeeseeks 131\nmeeseeks 196\nmeeseeks 262\nmeeseeks 392\n\n# Sum the summoned voices (Mix2Pcm is 2-in, so chain them), soften, echo, hold.\nfilter Mix2Pcm m1\nknob m1 normalize true\npatch 131 out_pcm -> m1 in_pcm_a\npatch 196 out_pcm -> m1 in_pcm_b\n\nfilter Mix2Pcm m2\nknob m2 normalize true\npatch m1 out_pcm -> m2 in_pcm_a\npatch 262 out_pcm -> m2 in_pcm_b\n\nfilter Mix2Pcm m3\nknob m3 normalize true\npatch m2 out_pcm -> m3 in_pcm_a\npatch 392 out_pcm -> m3 in_pcm_b\n\nfilter LowPass tone\nknob tone cutoff 1400.0\npatch m3 out_pcm -> tone in_pcm\n\nfilter Delay echo\nknob echo time 0.3\nknob echo feedback 0.35\nknob echo mix 0.25\npatch tone out_pcm -> echo in_pcm\n\nfilter Limiter lim\nknob lim ceiling 0.9\npatch echo out_pcm -> lim in_pcm\noutput lim out_pcm\n\npanel knob tone cutoff\npanel knob echo mix\n\n"+A.fr())},
